## Security checks and secrets

### Security checks in CI

Every push and pull request runs these checks; any HIGH or CRITICAL finding fails the build.

| Check | Tool | Fails when |
|---|---|---|
| Backend dependencies | `pip-audit -r requirements.txt` | any known vulnerability |
| Frontend dependencies | `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high` | a high or critical advisory in a runtime dependency |
| Images | Trivy (`--severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed`) | a fixable HIGH or CRITICAL vulnerability, or a secret, in either image |
| Committed secrets | `git ls-files` | a `.env` file is tracked |

Both images run as non-root users and contain no secrets.

### Where secrets live

| Environment | Store | How the app gets them |
|---|---|---|
| Local | `week-06-devops/backend/.env` (git-ignored, docker-ignored) | `env_file` in `docker-compose.yml` |
| CI | GitHub Actions secrets (`secrets.*`) | environment variables in the workflow |
| Production | AWS Secrets Manager | injected as environment variables by the container platform |

No secret is ever committed, baked into an image, or written to a log.
